PKG=zz9kbus46
NAME=zz9kbus-k46 1.0.0-1 - ZZ9000-family board registry module, k46 line
ARCH=Amiga
VERSION=1.0.0-1
CATEGORY=system
CLASSES=none
VENDOR=amix
PSTAMP=amix-zz9kbus46-1.0.0-1
# Kernel space (amix-dlm C2-2, C3-5 v4 sec 1): a role=module entry of the #ext kpkg block
# (line=k46), never an ordinary entry.  Catalog name zz9kbus-k46, pkginst zz9kbus46; VERSION
# is kernel/modules/zz9kbus/module/VERSION, the same on both lines.
APKG_DESC=The registry between ZZ9000-family board drivers (the Z3660's, a ZZ9000's) and the service channel zz9ksvc, as a boot-class kernel module for the 68040/68060 line module kernel kernel-k46-m: /etc/conf/mod.d/zz9kbus.
DESC=The kernel/modules zz9kbus module for the 68040/68060 line: a misc module of a few hundred bytes, boot class, resident on a box with a Z3660 or a ZZ9000 (match), loaded elsewhere when a board driver or zz9ksvc names it in depend.  Board drivers register the board they found; zz9ksvc takes it from here.  No device, no parameter.  /etc/conf/modreg.d/zz9kbus holds the package's defaults (none).  The package writes no boot store; after the install apkg runs kbootset build and commit (or prints the command when bootset=manual).  MIT.
